# WN22-DC-000080: Windows Server 2022 Active Directory SYSVOL directory must have the proper access control permissions.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: high
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-dc-000080-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `critical`

    title `Windows Server 2022 Active Directory SYSVOL directory must have the proper access control permissions.`
    description `Improper access permissions for directory data files could allow unauthorized users to read, modify, or delete directory data. The SYSVOL directory contains public files (to the domain) such as policies and logon scripts. Data in shared subdirectories are replicated to all domain controllers in a domain.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,high,file-acl,ntfs,ksi-iam-jit`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-JIT,NIST-800-53:AC-6(10)`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-JIT`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `1`
    recommendation `Maintain the permissions on the SYSVOL directory. Do not allow greater than "Read & execute" permissions for standard user accounts or groups. The defaults below meet this requirement: C:\Windows\SYSVOL Type - "Allow" for all Inherited from - "None" for all Principal - Access - Applies to Authenticated Users - Read & execute - This folder, subfolder, and files Server Operators - Read & execute- This folder, subfolder, and files Administrators - Special - This folder only (Special = Basic Permiss`

    component_id `comp-windows-file-acl`

    impl_KSI_IAM_JIT `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-JIT by asserting that the NTFS ACL on C:\Windows\SYSVOL does not grant any forbidden principal or rights combination, via Get-Acl through the windows_file_acl CTN. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_AC_6_10 `Windows Server implements AC-6(10) by asserting that the NTFS ACL on C:\Windows\SYSVOL does not grant any forbidden principal or rights combination, via Get-Acl through the windows_file_acl CTN. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        path `C:\Windows\SYSVOL`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE exists_check
        exists boolean = true
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_id_1
        allow_identities string not_contains `Everyone`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_id_2
        allow_identities string not_contains `Anonymous`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_id_3
        allow_identities string not_contains `Guest`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_1
        aces string not_contains `Authenticated Users|Allow|Modify`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_2
        aces string not_contains `Authenticated Users|Allow|FullControl`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_3
        aces string not_contains `Authenticated Users|Allow|Write`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_4
        aces string not_contains `BUILTIN\Users|Allow|Modify`
    STATE_END

    STATE forbid_ace_5
        aces string not_contains `BUILTIN\Users|Allow|FullControl`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF exists_check
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_id_1
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_id_2
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_id_3
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_1
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_2
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_3
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_4
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_file_acl
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF forbid_ace_5
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
